sentences.l:
So then he spoke, and to her wingless was the speech,
and she opened the doors of the well-inhabited halls,
and set out to go;

She found then Odysseus among the slain corpses,
spattered with blood and gore, like a lion
who, having eaten a field-dwelling ox, comes along;

Fifty, mark you, there are in the halls, women,
maidservants, whom we taught to do their tasks,
to card wool and to endure slavery;

First then the corpses they carried, the dead ones,
and down beneath the portico of the well-fenced courtyard they set them,
leaning them against one another;

But Telemachus and the cowherd and the swineherd
with scrapers the floor of the close-built house
scraped;

But come, to you a cloak and a tunic, clothes, let me bring,
and not thus in rags wrapped about, the broad shoulders,
stand in the halls;
